@datadog_agent.tf @vector.tf bugbot gave the following find, can you help? Vector module index access crashes when vector disabled

High Severity

When var.vector_dd_agent_logs_enabled is explicitly set to true while vector is disabled, module.vector[0].service_endpoint_dd_agent will cause an index-out-of-range error because module.vector has count = 0. The guard condition local.vector_dd_agent_logs_enabled does not guarantee module.vector has any instances. The rest of the codebase uses length(module.X) > 0 guards (e.g., cilium.tf) to safely access counted module outputs.

